<problem>
<!-- <title>Definite integral &#x2D; quadratic</title> -->

<setup>

<selectFromSequence name="aaa" from="-10" to="10" exclude="0" numToSelect="3" withReplacement="true" />

<function name="g" variables="t"><math simplify="numbersPreserveOrder">$aaa[1] *t^2+$aaa[2] *t+$aaa[3]</math></function>
<selectFromSequence name="lb" from="-2" to="1" />
<selectFromSequence name="ub" from="$lb+1" to="2" />

<function name="antideriv_g" simplify="numbers" symbolic="true" variables="t">$aaa[1]*t^3/3 + $aaa[2]*t^2/2 + $aaa[3]*t</function>
<math name="intgeval" simplify="numbers">$$antideriv_g($ub)-$$antideriv_g($lb)</math>


  

</setup>


<p>Evaluate the following integral:</p>
  
<p><m>\displaystyle \int_{$lb}^{$ub} $g \, dt =</m> 
<answer name="answer1" forceFullCheckworkButton="true">
<award allowedErrorInNumbers="0.0001">$intgeval </award>
<award credit="0.8" allowedErrorInNumbers="0.001" feedbackCodes="numericalerror">$intgeval </award>
</answer>
</p>
  $answer1.feedbacks

<p>
If rounding, include at least 5 significant digits in your response.
</p>

<solution>

<setup>
  <function name="indefinta" variables="t" simplify="numbers" symbolic="true">t^3/3</function>
<evaluate name="indefinta_ub" function="$indefinta" input="$ub" />
<evaluate name="indefinta_lb" function="$indefinta" input="$lb" />
<function name="indefintb" variables="t" simplify="numbers" symbolic="true">t^2/2</function>
<evaluate name="indefintb_ub" function="$indefintb" input="$ub" />
<evaluate name="indefintb_lb" function="$indefintb" input="$lb" />
<function name="indefintc" variables="t" simplify="numbers" symbolic="true">t</function>
<evaluate name="indefintc_ub" function="$indefintc" input="$ub" />
<evaluate name="indefintc_lb" function="$indefintc" input="$lb" />

<math name="intsevalpart"> $aaa[1] *($indefinta_ub -$indefinta_lb )+$aaa[2] *($indefintb_ub -$indefintb_lb )+$aaa[3] *($indefintc_ub -$indefintc_lb ) </math>

<math name="intseval"> <math simplify="numbers">$aaa[1] *($indefinta_ub -$indefinta_lb )</math>+<math simplify="numbers">$aaa[2] *($indefintb_ub -$indefintb_lb )</math>+<math simplify="numbers">$aaa[3] *($indefintc_ub -$indefintc_lb )</math> </math>

</setup>

<p>We first use the sum and constant product rules for integration: 
</p>
  
<p>
<m>\displaystyle \int_{$lb}^{$ub} $g \, dt 
 =$aaa[1] \int_{$lb}^{$ub} t^2 \,dt
 +$aaa[2] \int_{$lb}^{$ub} t \,dt
 +$aaa[3] \int_{$lb}^{$ub} 1 \,dt
</m>
</p>

<p>

We then evaluate each of these integrals using the power rule for integration:
</p>
  
<p>
<m>\displaystyle 
  $aaa[1] \frac{t^3}{3}\bigg|_{$lb}^{$ub}
  +$aaa[2] \frac{t^2}{2}\bigg|_{$lb}^{$ub}
  +$aaa[3] t\bigg|_{$lb}^{$ub}
</m>
</p>
<p>
Finally, we substitute in the bounds and simplify:
</p>

<p>
<m>\displaystyle $intsevalpart = $intseval  = $intgeval </m>
</p>


</solution>


</problem>